  "status": "COMPLETE",
  "verdict": "PASS (sanity + F-Heads + F-Selective)",
  "findings": {
   "sanity": "The noising estimator recovers the known reader: L3H1 carries 0.782 of the coupling, the max of all scanned heads. L2H15 (the addresser) noises to only 0.011 on its own -- its effect is mediated through L3H1, not carried directly -- and L1H12 to ~0. Estimator trustworthy.",
   "relays": "Three layer-4/5 relay heads clear CI-low > 0.05: L5H11 (0.125), L4H2 (0.122), L4H0 (0.081). A distributed TAIL of smaller contributors (L4H13/L4H11/L4H4/L5H9, ~0.03-0.04, CI-low > 0 but < 0.05) sits below the relay threshold: the L4/L5 relay is a head-sparse CORE plus a distributed tail, not exactly three heads.",
   "router_vs_transporter": "All three relays are TRANSPORTERS. Noising the VALUE destroys the coupling (0.142, 0.123, 0.082); noising QUERY+KEY destroys ~0 (-0.001, -0.002, -0.002). So the heads carry the acceptor-dependent U_info CONTENT through OV/value, while their attention routing is acceptor-INDEPENDENT (fixed/positional). Clean, unambiguous split.",
   "general_purpose": "Descriptive (mean-ablation health): all three relays drop general masked-MLM to ~0.51, i.e. they are GENERAL-PURPOSE heads that also carry the coupling, not dedicated splice heads. SpliceBERT reuses shared positional-mixing machinery."
  },
  "intent_check": {
   "closes_forward_arm_part2": true,
   "summary": "Prompt forward-arm part 2 ('which L4/L5 heads receive those directions through Q/K/V/OV') is answered: L5H11, L4H2, L4H0 receive U_info through the VALUE/OV path (transporters), not QK. The meet-in-the-middle is now closed at the head level: L3H1 write (donor+/-5) -> MLP3/MLP4 assemble U_info -> {L4H0, L4H2, L5H11} transport the U_info content via OV to the donor -> U_info reads out -> donor-G logit."
  },
  "escaped_failure_modes": {
   "checked": [
    "Mean-ablation-not-noising trap (R12/R13): avoided by NOISING-to-corrupt, which changes only the acceptor-dependent part of a head's output. Confirmed selective: only 3 of 32 L4/L5 heads clear the relay bar; a global-breakage artifact would flag ~all of them.",
    "The QK/OV split is not near-tautological: damage_QK is ~0 (not just < damage_V), so the attention pattern genuinely carries none of the acceptor dependence.",
    "Sanity anchors the estimator (L3H1 tops at 0.782), so the L4/L5 numbers are read on a scale where the known reader behaves as expected."
   ],
   "residual_risk": "(1) The QK/OV noising was applied at ALL positions (coarse). 'These are positional gatherers attending donor->flank' is a plausible reading of QK-independence but the attention-pattern geometry (does the head actually attend the donor to the donor+/-5 flank where MLP3/MLP4 assembled U_info) was NOT measured -- a descriptive follow-up. (2) The head-sparse core has a distributed tail, so 'three heads' is the core, not the whole L4/L5 contribution. (3) The relays being general-purpose means the circuit is not a set of dedicated units; completeness at the head level is bounded, like C7."
  },
  "next_step": "1e -- the causal signature of U_info: what information does it actually encode (paired -acceptor vs generic splice-site evidence, coding vs noncoding context, splice phase), now that the object and its full L3H1->MLP->transporter->readout path are mapped. Optional descriptive add: the donor->flank attention geometry of the three transporters."
 }
